@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### Registrar usuario normal
# @name registerUser
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "name": "Ana Torres",
  "email": "ana@example.com",
  "password": "una frase de acceso segura"
}

### Login de usuario normal
# @name loginUser
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "ana@example.com",
  "password": "una frase de acceso segura"
}

### Extraer token de Ana
@userToken = {{loginUser.response.body.accessToken}}

### Perfil de Ana
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Buscar ciudades cuyo nombre contiene "mad" (guarda /api/cities sin query string)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cities?search=mad
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Listar ciudades con aeropuertos
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cities/with-airports
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Listar aeropuertos de París (id 3 en los datos iniciales)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cities/3/airports
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Ana, que es usuario normal, no puede crear una ciudad: debe responder 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/cities
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "name": "Valencia",
  "country": "España"
}

### Login de administración
# @name loginAdmin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@aeropuertos.test",
  "password": "password"
}

### Extraer token de administrador
@adminToken = {{loginAdmin.response.body.accessToken}}

### El administrador crea Valencia
# @name createCity
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/cities
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "name": "Valencia",
  "country": "España"
}

### Extraer id de la ciudad creada
@valenciaId = {{createCity.response.body.id}}

### El administrador añade el aeropuerto de Valencia
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/airports
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "iataCode": "VLC",
  "name": "Aeropuerto de Valencia",
  "cityId": {{valenciaId}}
}

### ==========================================
### COMPROBACIONES DE AUDITORÍA (U01_05_07)
### ==========================================
@anaId = {{loginUser.response.body.user.id}}
@adminId = {{loginAdmin.response.body.user.id}}

### Registrar un usuario nuevo sin actividad previa para probar array vacío []
# @name registerEmptyUser
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "name": "Usuario Sin Logs",
  "email": "sinlogs@example.com",
  "password": "una frase de acceso segura"
}

@emptyUserId = {{registerEmptyUser.response.body.id}}

### 1. Petición sin autenticación -> 401 (no genera registro de auditoría)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/cities
Accept: application/json

### 2. Consulta admin sin autenticar -> 401 (no genera registro de auditoría)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/users/{{anaId}}/logs
Accept: application/json

### 3. Usuario normal consulta ruta admin -> 403 (registra 403 para Ana)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/users/{{anaId}}/logs
Authorization: Bearer {{userToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 4. Admin consulta historial completo de Ana -> 200 (más reciente primero)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/users/{{anaId}}/logs
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 5. Admin consulta con n=2 -> 200 (máximo 2 registros más recientes)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/users/{{anaId}}/logs?n=2
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 6. Admin consulta con n=1 -> 200 (solo el registro más reciente)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/users/{{anaId}}/logs?n=1
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Registrar usuario sin actividad previa (cambia el email si ya lo usaste antes)
# @name registerEmptyUser
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "name": "Usuario Sin Logs",
  "email": "sinlogs.prueba1@example.com",
  "password": "una frase de acceso segura"
}

@emptyUserId = {{registerEmptyUser.response.body.id}}

### 7. Admin consulta usuario existente sin registros -> 200 y []
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/users/{{emptyUserId}}/logs
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Accept: application/json
### 8. Admin consulta usuario inexistente -> 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/users/999999/logs
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 9. Parámetro n no entero positivo (n=0) -> 422
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/users/{{anaId}}/logs?n=0
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 10. Parámetro n no entero positivo (n=-3) -> 422
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/users/{{anaId}}/logs?n=-3
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 11. Parámetro n no entero positivo (n=abc) -> 422
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/users/{{anaId}}/logs?n=abc
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 12. Admin consulta su propia actividad -> 200 (debe incluir las consultas anteriores a /logs)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/users/{{adminId}}/logs
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
Accept: application/json